# Infect is a static ability (CR 702.90a), and the -1/-1 counters its damage puts on a creature (CR 120.3d, 702.90c) are
# that ability's effect (CR 609.1: static abilities create effects), combat damage's as much as an effect's damage: the
# turn-based action deals the damage, and infect decides what it does. So Doubling Season doubles them ("if an effect would
# put one or more counters on a permanent you control"). Glistener Elf attacks into Bot2's Picklock Prankster (1/3) under
# Bot2's Doubling Season: the Prankster gets two -1/-1 counters, not one, and is a -1/1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Glistener Elf
Forest x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Doubling Season
Picklock Prankster
Mox Sapphire
Island x12

